.Dd February 11, 2026
.Dt VOP_CLOSE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_close
.Nd close a vnode and release open state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In vfs/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_close "struct vnode *vp" "int fflag" "struct ucred *cred"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_close
wrapper delegates close handling to the filesystem callback and updates vnode
open/write counters.
When the final writer is released,
.Fn vop_fsync
is invoked with synchronous semantics so dirty data is flushed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error number on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EIO
I/O synchronization failed during last-close flush.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The operation is not supported for the vnode.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_open 9 ,
.Xr vop_fsync 9
